    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1197-a3">

                <pb facs="0968" n="852" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg852"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3—Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Commander Kavanagh to
                        Consul Alger</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>U. S. S. “<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Annapolis</hi>,”</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 22, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Villistas and Indians have again raided Los Mochis, burning several large
                    residences, looting and wrecking all others, pillaging all warehouses, driving
                    off all live stock. Several Mexicans have been killed, a number of Mexican women
                    have been carried off or outraged. All Americans and a great number of Mexicans
                    have fled here for safety as a reign of terror exists. Please lay these matters
                    before General Muñoz and very strongly and insistently request that he
                    immediately send a sufficient force of troops to protect lives and property and
                    to fix a definite time when these troops are to be expected here.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kavanagh.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
